With the original data set,

ggplot(d.p, aes(x=K, y=err, group=I, colour=ordered(I))) +  geom_line() +

 scale_colour_hue(limits=c(-.4, 0))

produces a plot with two lines (for -.4 and 0) and a legend with three
entries (for -.4, -.2, and 0); the .-2 legend box has no line drawn
through it.  This doesn't seem like it can possibly be what anyone
wants.

zw

